                        "entry_id": "9bf7c829-0adf-318f-b9a0-50bca93e2b17",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A poor or lazy hand on a sailing vessel."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8ca9b981-2324-47bd-b834-c988476942fa",
                                "sense_id": "776146c3-528f-36c3-a0b2-6dfaef420b7c",
                                "text": "The captain called him a \"soger,\" and promised to \"ride him down as he would the main tack;\" and when officers are once determined to \"ride a man down,\" it is a gone case with him."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f1bde50e-f2f6-4fff-9310-570754b0563c",
                                "sense_id": "776146c3-528f-36c3-a0b2-6dfaef420b7c",
                                "text": "I'd hang a lazy soger / The same as any other."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9d15ff51-7cda-4656-b5cb-34e5e6df3518",
                                "sense_id": "776146c3-528f-36c3-a0b2-6dfaef420b7c",
                                "text": "Come aft, you lazy soger, an' see what de captain has to say 'bout dis,\" cried Worcester, pushing the man, who still grasped his knife, before him […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
